//? Title: Token bucket: actual lazy refill and caller-clock admission
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A token bucket banks a finite burst allowance and refills at a configured rate.
Actual before/refill/admission/after states explain the original five-token
burst and six subsequent requests.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

At nondecreasing caller time t, credit=min(capacity,tokens+(t-last)*rate), then
admit a nonnegative cost only if the credit covers it. Admission subtracts the
cost; denial still retains refill credit and advances the clock. Starting full
gives the exact-arithmetic envelope admitted cost<=capacity+rate*elapsed; double
rounding qualifies exact numerical boundary interpretations. This is a meter:
denied requests are returned immediately rather than queued. No wall clock,
scheduler, network shaping or synchronization is implied.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/token_bucket_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    a::TokenBucket bucket(2, 1);
    std::vector<a::TokenBucketStep> r{bucket.consume(0), bucket.consume(0),
                                      bucket.consume(0), bucket.consume(.5),
                                      bucket.consume(1)};
    std::print("| actual time | stored before | refill added | available | cost | admitted | stored after " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.time, s.before,
                   s.refilled, s.available, s.cost, s.consumed, s.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0},
                         "Actual capacity2 and refill1 per time unit");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual admission operations", r.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual final tokens {}",
                                     bucket.stored_tokens()));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/token_bucket_tiny.svg");
}
```
